{"name":"Carousel Pink","hex":"#f8dbe0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carousel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pleasure ride, typically found at amusement parks and fairs and accompanied by music, consisting of a slowly revolving circular platform on which are fixed various seats, frequently shaped like horses or other animals, cars, etc., which may also move up and down; a merry-go-round.","A revolving device for item delivery or display."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To revolve or change places."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carousel"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carousel","blocks":[{"text":"A carousel or carrousel, merry-go-round, flying horses, or galloper is a type of amusement ride consisting of a rotating circular platform with seats for riders. The seats are traditionally in the form of rows of animal figures mounted on posts, many of which move up and down to simulate galloping. Sometimes chair-like or bench-like seats are used, and occasionally mounts can take the form of non-animals, such as airplanes or cars. Carousel rides are typically accompanied by looped circus music."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/A_double-decker_carousel_in_Milton_Keynes%2C_England_at_Christmas.jpg/330px-A_double-decker_carousel_in_Milton_Keynes%2C_England_at_Christmas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carousel"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Man%C3%A8geLR1.jpg/500px-Man%C3%A8geLR1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Man%C3%A8geLR1.jpg/1280px-Man%C3%A8geLR1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Man%C3%A8geLR1.jpg/500px-Man%C3%A8geLR1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A double-decker carousel in France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMan%C3%A8geLR1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Carrousel-LouisXIV-1662.jpg/500px-Carrousel-LouisXIV-1662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Carrousel-LouisXIV-1662.jpg/1280px-Carrousel-LouisXIV-1662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Carrousel-LouisXIV-1662.jpg/500px-Carrousel-LouisXIV-1662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A carrousel tournament organized in the Tuileries Palace courtyard by Louis XIV in 1662 to celebrate the birth of his son and heir. This event and others like it inspired the creation of the carousel amusement ride.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarrousel-LouisXIV-1662.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c